    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Chap 670 of 2022",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8409\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 670 of the laws of 2022 amending the real prop-\nerty tax law relating to providing all local governments with the option\nto provide a property tax exemption to volunteer firefighters and volun-\nteer ambulance workers, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to amend Chapter 670 of the laws of 2022 by\nextending the effective date of section two of the act by three years.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends Chapter 670 of the laws of 2022 by extending the effec-\ntive date of section two of the act by three years.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nChapter 670 of the laws of 2022 established RPTL Sec. 466-a*, a state-\nwide volunteer firefighter/ambulance worker exemption intended to\nreplace the numerous local bills authorizing such exemptions in various\nlocalities. Chapter 670 sets those local exemption bills to expire in\n2025. This bill extends the local bills until 2028 to allow munici-\npalities that have not adopted a local law to replace them under RPTL\nSec. 466-a*.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
